            <div xml:id="d47">

                <pb facs="0053" n="41" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg41"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851G.00/5–1446: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Hanoi</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">O’Sullivan</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hanoi</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-05-14T08:00:00+07:00">May 14, 1946—8
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 15—3:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>14. Chinese have officially informed French that withdrawal offers [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">orders?</hi>] have been recd. French state that
                    according to information given them Chinese withdrawal will commence May 15 and
                    will be completed by June 10. French also state their forces were scheduled to
                    enter Luang Prabang yesterday noon. French column entering that city was
                    reinforced during last few days with paratroopers.</p>
                <closer>[<signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">O’Sullivan</hi></signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
